{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506213-do-you-need-a-soul-to-make-a-soul-stone","id":1506213,"title":"Do you need a soul to make a soul stone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-22T22:38:18-07:00","id":1506213,"title":"Do you need a soul to make a soul stone?","content":"By RAW, there's no mention that you need a soul to make one, as you imprint your Nimbus onto something and being soulless doesn't prevent you from doing that.<br /> <br /> However, a lot of stuff in Mage 2e about soul stones mention that soul stones contain part of the creator's soul (though very little; Tremere can't feed on the sliver in it for any amount of time, and even a Hollow 10 Tremere can feed on a Sleeper soul for an entire day, let alone an Awakened one).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T23:13:50-07:00","id":1506214,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m inclined to say that you do need a soul, though this means I\u2019ll have to think a bit about the part where you can create soul stones without having a soul\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T23:21:45-07:00","id":1506215,"title":"","content":"The idea that there are thirty mage books, but none of them say that you need a soul to make a soulstone is a bit unbelievable to me. Are you sure about that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T23:32:51-07:00","id":1506217,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly, the creation process for soulstones doesn't seem to come up much. Mechanically we know it's a thing, but it's the uses that come up more often than the actual creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T03:16:01-07:00","id":1506220,"title":"","content":"I would say that you don't. But only because you can still cast spells without a soul (so long as you aren't in the last stage of soul lose and have lost all your Gnosis).<br /> <br /> That means there is enough &quot;Ummphf&quot; left that even without a soul you can still imprint your soul's identity into a soulstone. Still enough of a connection to the Supernal...<br /> <br /> But that is all temporary, quantum entanglement with your soul perhaps, which (unless you use time to prevent the Soulless condition getting worse, looking at you Veil of Moments) will evapourate as soon as they lose their will to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T05:54:48-07:00","id":1506227,"title":"","content":"A soul stone is technically a misnomer. It contains a severed piece of the mage's Gnosis, which is a direct gateway to their soul.<br /> <br /> With that being said, page 186 of <i>Summoners</i> has an alternative in the form of a Supernal Anchor. It binds a compliant or defeated Supernal Entity into a stable vessel, stopping corrosion and allowing them to act as a soul stone. Its requires quite a bit of power to pull off (Gnosis 5), plus work to summon and bind them. Its highly Hubristic, since you are placing a Supernal Entity in the Fallen, where it can be consumed or corrupted, but it is an alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T05:28:45-07:00","id":1506743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506213-do-you-need-a-soul-to-make-a-soul-stone?p=1506227#post1506227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A soul stone is technically a misnomer. It contains a severed piece of the mage's Gnosis, which is a direct gateway to their soul.<br /> <br /> With that being said, page 186 of <i>Summoners</i> has an alternative in the form of a Supernal Anchor. It binds a compliant or defeated Supernal Entity into a stable vessel, stopping corrosion and allowing them to act as a soul stone. Its requires quite a bit of power to pull off (Gnosis 5), plus work to summon and bind them. Its highly Hubristic, since you are placing a Supernal Entity in the Fallen, where it can be consumed or corrupted, but it is an alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e though, a LOT of mentions about soul stones say that there are bits of soul in it. Not much - as I said, the Tremere section says that it's not even remotely enough to feed on, so the amount must be minuscule indeed. Probably you need the soul shaving as tape or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T09:22:57-07:00","id":1506753,"title":"","content":"I think when the definition given for a soul stone is &quot;the mage places a piece of their Awakened soul into an object&quot;, it can be inferred that the soul must be present. Don't forget that the process isn't just about imprinting one's Nimbus, it also costs a Willpower dot, which tends to represent investing a bit of oneself into something.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable for the word count to have stated that to have been low priority.<br /> <br /> Although it also sounds like a low priority in character terms as well; I would feel that, if your soul has been taken, making soul stones would be the last thing on your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T10:22:07-07:00","id":1506759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's reasonable for the word count to have stated that to have been low priority. </div> </div> </div>I agree. Much of the metaphysics of Mage, (and the rest of the CofD) that has built up over the years is pretty dense, and not the kind of thing you want dumped in a core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506213-do-you-need-a-soul-to-make-a-soul-stone?p=1506753#post1506753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although it also sounds like a low priority in character terms as well; I would feel that, if your soul has been taken, making soul stones would be the last thing on your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had that same thought, although, your soul returned in exchange for a soul stone sounds like a pretty classic Awakening scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T10:23:09-07:00","id":1506760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1506213-do-you-need-a-soul-to-make-a-soul-stone?p=1506753#post1506753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think when the definition given for a soul stone is &quot;the mage places a piece of their Awakened soul into an object&quot;, it can be inferred that the soul must be present. Don't forget that the process isn't just about imprinting one's Nimbus, it also costs a Willpower dot, which tends to represent investing a bit of oneself into something.<br /> <br /> I think it's reasonable for the word count to have stated that to have been low priority.<br /> <br /> Although it also sounds like a low priority in character terms as well; I would feel that, if your soul has been taken, making soul stones would be the last thing on your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How did Macaria become a Mad One, again?&quot; the apprentice asked.<br /> <br /> &quot;She put her soul in a locked box and then tried to make a soul stone without it.&quot; the mentor said.<br /> <br /> &quot;But why?&quot; the apprentice asked.<br /> <br /> &quot;Because it would have been cool if it worked.&quot; the mentor said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","user":"jsnider3","date":". 04-12-2023, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}